employment of $P T S A.H_{2}O$ during the slow baking process resulted in an extensive increment in the crystallinity and the porosity of the resulting framework structure， alongside entrapment of the mediator molecules as proton conductors inside the ordered pore channels. These COFMs show super protonic conductivity， as high as $7.8\times10^{-2}$ S cm-1 (PTSA@TpAzo） at $80^{\circ}$ Cunder $95\%$ relative humidity and could be observed faring better amongst the prevailing crystalline porous organic polymer-based proton conducting materials. It is important to note that the preliminary studies indicate an increase in the proton conductivity with decrease in the thickness.However, we could use membranes (PTSA@COFMs) onlyup to $105\upmu\mathrm{m}$ thickness in this study.Thus, conspicuously,it could be expected that a PTSA@COFM with a thickness of $\mathtt{\le50}$ μm could render a single cell performance very close to that of the state of the art Nafion° based PEMFC.
